From 702b76d875335234740092ac41bfb1861233190f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:28:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: record phase timings, and summarize them with
 --phase-report

Measurement only; no behaviour change.

With --phasedir=DIR, each test writes DIR/<script>.<pid>.json on exit,
on success and on failure. It holds the wall-clock duration of these
phases:
- chain_init: cache copy or clean-chain setup;
- network_setup;
- body;
- final_stop;
- cleanup.

It also holds every node start (process spawn until RPC is ready) and
node stop, and the time spent in sync_blocks, sync_mempools and
sync_proofs.

test_runner.py --phase-report passes --phasedir and prints:
- totals per phase;
- node start and stop counts and means;
- sync wait totals and their share of body time;
- the 20 tests with the most setup/teardown and with the longest body.

The raw data is written to <tmpdir>/phase-report.json.

First full-suite report (macOS arm64, -j 12, load average 27-35):
- body: 3461 s;
- node starts: 574 s (752 starts, mean 763 ms);
- node stops: 265 s;
- sync_blocks: 307 s (1274 calls, mean 241 ms);
- sync_mempools: 94 s;
- sync_proofs: 33 s.
